From: Mahdi Arts <mahdi-arts@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ci: activate hardened CI/release/E2E workflows (SHA-pinned, supply-chain gates)

Activation patch for the hardened, canonical-named pipelines. This PR's
bot token cannot push `.github/workflows/*` (GitHub Apps need the
`workflows` permission), so the workflow files travel as this patch —
the single maintainer activation step:

پچ فعال‌سازی خطوط لولهٔ hardened و نام‌گذاری‌شدهٔ رسمی. توکن ربات این PR
نمی‌تواند `.github/workflows/*` را پوش کند (GitHub App به مجوز `workflows`
نیاز دارد)، پس فایل‌های ورک‌فلو با همین پچ حمل می‌شوند — تک‌گام فعال‌سازی
برای نگهدارنده:

    git am docs/patches/hardened-ci-workflows.patch
    git push    # needs a workflows-scoped token or direct maintainer push

Contents / محتوا:
  - ci.yml:      canonical names, rustup (no third-party Rust action),
                 packaging job incl. flatpak-builder-lint (SHA-pinned)
  - release.yml: canonical artifact names/URLs/AUR, optional GPG/SBOM/SLSA
  - e2e.yml:     NEW manual Playwright workflow (webkit/chromium/firefox)
  - stale.yml:   actions/stale pinned to a full commit SHA

Applies cleanly on master and on this branch (workflow files are the
patch's only subject). After `git am`, `.github/workflows/` is the single
source of truth and this patch becomes historical (archive it in
docs/archive/patches/). Superseded patches already live there.

---
